      "title": "A guide to Old English pronunciation",
      "master_sha256": "7c6b8e6907962362381148b077dbbbb23b6fbe4196f98064faef00d2988ec346",
      "prose_blocks": 88,
      "tables": [
        {
          "id": "T01",
          "headers": [
            "Letters",
            "Short vowel",
            "Long vowel"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "a, ā",
              "The vowel of *father*, brief: **ac**, “but”.",
              "Hold the same vowel: **āc**, “oak”."
            ],
            [
              "æ, ǣ",
              "The vowel of *cat*: **sæt**, “sat”.",
              "Hold that same vowel: **sǣd**, “seed”."
            ],
            [
              "e, ē",
              "The vowel of *bet*: **męte**, “food”.",
              "Hold the beginning of *day* without its final glide: **hē**, “he”."
            ],
            [
              "i, ī",
              "The vowel of *bit*: **is**, “is”.",
              "The vowel of *see*, held: **īs**, “ice”."
            ],
            [
              "o, ō",
              "A brief rounded vowel, described below: **god**, “god”.",
              "Hold the beginning of *go* without its final glide: **gōd**, “good”."
            ],
            [
              "u, ū",
              "The vowel of *foot*: **full**, “full”.",
              "The vowel of *food*, held: **fūl**, “vile”."
            ],
            [
              "y, ȳ",
              "The tongue position of *bit* with rounded lips: **wyrt**, “herb; plant”.",
              "The tongue position of *see* with rounded lips, held: **fȳr**, “fire”."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "T02",
          "headers": [
            "Spellings",
            "Movement",
            "Supplied examples"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "ea, ēa",
              "Start with the vowel of *cat*, then round toward **oo**.",
              "**earm**, “arm”; **ēare**, “ear”."
            ],
            [
              "eo, ēo",
              "Start with the steady first vowel of *day*, then round toward **oo**.",
              "**eorl**, “man”; **fēoll**, “fell”."
            ],
            [
              "ie, īe",
              "Start with the vowel of *see*, then round toward **oo**.",
              "**giefan**, “give”; **hīeran**, “hear”."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "T03",
          "headers": [
            "Spelling",
            "Sound",
            "Supplied examples and limits"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "c",
              "**k** as in *kit*, or **ch** as in *chin*.",
              "**cuman**, “come”, begins with **k**. Both **c** letters in **cyrice**, “church”, are **ch**."
            ],
            [
              "c before a front vowel",
              "Often **ch**, but not invariably.",
              "**cēlan**, “cool”, begins with **k**, despite **ē**."
            ],
            [
              "g at the beginning",
              "Hard **g** as in *go*, or consonant **y** as in *yes*.",
              "**god**, “god”, has hard **g**; **giefan**, “give”, begins with **y**."
            ],
            [
              "g elsewhere",
              "Consonant **y**, or the continuous sound described below; some contexts retain hard **g**.",
              "**dæg**, “day”, ends with **y**; **fugol**, “bird”, has continuous **g**."
            ],
            [
              "sc",
              "Usually **sh** as in *ship*.",
              "**scip**, “ship”, has one **sh** sound; **frosc**, “frog”, instead ends with **s** followed by **k**."
            ],
            [
              "cg; usually gg",
              "The final sound of *bridge*.",
              "**ecg**, “edge”. The supplied exception **docga**, “dog”, has a prolonged hard **g**."
            ],
            [
              "ng",
              "Usually as in *finger*, with audible **g**.",
              "**lang**, “long”. In **sengan**, “singe”, **ng** instead has the sound at the end of *singe*."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "T04",
          "headers": [
            "Word",
            "Meaning",
            "Sound to use"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "cnīf",
              "knife",
              "Final **f** as in *fan*."
            ],
            [
              "cnīfas",
              "knives",
              "**f** as in *van*, between vowels; final **s** as in *sip*."
            ],
            [
              "rīsan",
              "rise",
              "**s** as in *zip*, between vowels."
            ],
            [
              "hūs",
              "house",
              "Final **s** as in *sip*."
            ],
            [
              "ōðer",
              "other",
              "**ð** as in *this*, between vowels."
            ],
            [
              "ðā",
              "then",
              "Initial **ð** as in *thin*."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "T05",
          "headers": [
            "Word",
            "Supplied meaning",
            "Pronunciation help"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "God",
              "God",
              "One syllable; hard **g** and short rounded **o**."
            ],
            [
              "gescēop",
              "created",
              "Two syllables; stress the second. Initial **g** is **y** as in *yes*; **sc** is **sh**. Keep the first **e** light, and make long **ēo** one glide."
            ],
            [
              "heofonan",
              "heaven",
              "Three syllables; stress the first. **eo** is one short glide; **f** is voiced, as in *van*. Keep both following vowel syllables."
            ],
            [
              "and",
              "and",
              "A light connective; keep the final **d** audible."
            ],
            [
              "eorðan",
              "earth",
              "Two syllables; stress the first. **eo** is one short glide; **ð** is voiced, as in *this*. Keep the final **-an** audible."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
